sec.p:
After the injection, all eggs were returned to the incubator. On day 18 of incubation, eggs were transferred to hatching trays. The hatch was monitored from day 20 to day 22. A chick was regarded as hatched when it had completely left the shell and displayed no gross abnormality. Percentage hatchability was determined for each group using the formula:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\mathrm{Hatchability}}\left( \% \right) = \left( {{\mathrm{Total}}\;{\mathrm{number}}\;{\mathrm{of}}\;{\mathrm{hatched}}\;{\mathrm{chicks}}/{\mathrm{Total}}\;{\mathrm{number}}\;{\mathrm{of}}\;{\mathrm{fertile}}\;{\mathrm{eggs}}\;{\mathrm{set}}} \right) \times {1}00.$$\end{document}

After hatching, chicks were labeled and weighed individually to the nearest 0.1 g. Chick yield was calculated for each group according to the following equation:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\mathrm{Chick}}\;{\mathrm{yield}}\% = {\mathrm{Average}}\;{\mathrm{chick}}\;{\mathrm{weight}}/{\mathrm{Average}}\;{\mathrm{egg}}\;{\mathrm{weight}}\;{\mathrm{at}}\;{\mathrm{setting}} \times {1}00.$$\end{document}
